## 📁 Repository Structure

```
opspilot/
├── pyproject.toml               # Package config & dependencies
├── README.md                    # System documentation
├── ARCHITECTURE.md              # Architectural specification & safeguards
├── Makefile                     # Standard development commands
├── config/
│   └── llm_config.yaml          # Model parameters, timeouts, budget B
├── src/
│   └── opspilot/
│       ├── __init__.py
│       ├── cli.py               # CLI entrypoint
│       ├── analysis/            # Phase 1: Parsers & AST Extraction
│       │   ├── parsers/
│       │   │   ├── cobol_parser.py
│       │   │   ├── plsql_parser.py
│       │   │   └── tree_sitter_utils.py
│       │   ├── dependency_graph.py
│       │   └── analysis_agent.py
│       ├── orchestration/       # Phase 2: Master Control Plane
│       │   ├── master_orchestrator.py
│       │   └── pipeline_state.py
│       ├── execution/           # Phase 3: Bounded Coder-Verifier Loop
│       │   ├── coder_agent.py
│       │   ├── verifier_agent.py
│       │   ├── self_refine_loop.py
│       │   └── refine_rl/       # OpsPilot+: predictive iteration budget (Idea 8)
│       ├── governance/          # Phase 4: Deterministic Guardrails
│       │   ├── guardrail_rules.py
│       │   ├── guardrail_interceptor.py
│       │   └── sentinel_policy/ # OpsPilot+: adaptive guardrail thresholds (Idea 2)
│       ├── memory/              # OpsPilot+: repo-scale memory & propagation (Idea 4)
│       └── utils/               # Infrastructure & Logging
│           ├── logging_utils.py
│           └── json_schema.py
├── docs/
│   ├── IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md  # Advisor rationale: scope, decisions, honest results
│   ├── EVALUATION_RESULTS.md    # Reproducible evaluation numbers + plots
│   └── results/                 # Generated plots and raw evaluation JSON/CSV
├── workspace/                   # Sandboxed execution workspace
├── tests/                       # Complete pytest suite (59 tests)
└── examples/
    └── sample_legacy/
        ├── PAYROLL.CBL          # COBOL sample source
        └── ORDERS.SQL           # PL/SQL sample source
```

---

## ⚙️ Setup & Installation

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.10+
- (Optional) Docker for containerized verification sandbox

### Virtual Environment Setup
```bash
python -m venv .venv
# On Windows:
.\.venv\Scripts\activate
# On Linux/macOS:
source .venv/bin/activate

pip install -e .[dev]
```

### Environment Variables
Set your LLM provider configuration (OpenAI / Azure / Custom):
```bash
export OPENAI_API_KEY="your-api-key"
```

---

## 🛠️ Usage

### Analyze Legacy Code (Phase 1 Only)
```bash
python -m opspilot.cli analyze examples/sample_legacy/PAYROLL.CBL
```

### Run Full Modernization Pipeline
```bash
python -m opspilot.cli run-pipeline examples/sample_legacy/PAYROLL.CBL
```

### Running via Makefile
```bash
make analyze FILE=examples/sample_legacy/PAYROLL.CBL
make run-pipeline FILE=examples/sample_legacy/ORDERS.SQL
make test
make lint
```

### Run an OpsPilot+ extension evaluation
```bash
python -m opspilot.cli evaluate-extensions all --output-dir workspace/extension_eval
# or individually:
python -m opspilot.cli evaluate-extensions sentinel_policy
python -m opspilot.cli evaluate-extensions refine_rl
python -m opspilot.cli evaluate-extensions repo_mind
```

### Enable an extension in the live pipeline
Set `extensions.<name>.enabled: true` in `config/llm_config.yaml`, then run
`run-pipeline` as usual. See `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md` for what each
extension does when active.

---

## 🧪 Testing

Run all unit and integration tests:
```bash
pytest -v tests/
```
